$DATUM Methyl
2-((2R,5S,6S)-6-((2E,8E,10S,11R,12R)-12-((tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy)-11-methoxy-
6,8,10-trimethyltrideca-2,4,8-trien-2-yl)-5-methyltetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)acetate
(20a). A solution of the sulfone 19 (219 mg, 0.408 mmol) was dissolved in
anhydrous THF (5 mL) and cooled to -78 °C (bath temperature). This
solution was then slowly treated with a solution of KHMDS (751 mL, 0.5 M
in toluene); during the addition the solution turned yellow. This
solution was allowed to stir for 1h at -78 °C and was then slowly treated
with a solution of the aldehyde 16a (75 mg, 0.313 mmol) in anhydrous THF
(5 mL). The resulting mixture was allowed to stir at this temperature for
an additional 1.5 h then quenched with sat aqueous solution of NH4Cl (10
mL), allowed to warm to ambient temperature and stir for 10 min. The
mixture was extracted with EtOAc, washed with brine, dried, filtered and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The resulting residue was purified
by flash chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexanes, 1:10). The title
compound as an inseparable mixture of E and Z isomers (7:2) (942 mg, 92%)
as a colorless oil. [α]D= -0.92 (c = 1.18, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 6.11 (ddd, J = 15.3, 10.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.84 (dd, J = 10.9, 1.8
Hz, 1H), 5.47 (dd, J = 15.0, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.06 (dd, J = 9.3, 1.8 Hz, 1H),
3.82 - 3.65 (m, 2H), 3.60 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 3H), 3.38 (s, 3H), 3.26 (d, J =
9.9 Hz, 1H), 2.71 (dd, J = 6.3, 4.5 Hz, 1H), 2.60 - 2.43 (m, 2H), 2.33
(ddd, J = 14.0, 7.1, 2.5 Hz, 2H), 1.99 - 1.70 (m, 3H), 1.62-1.65 (m, 5H),
1.53 (t, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 1.51 (s, 3H), 1.35 - 1.10 (m, 4H), 1.06 (d, J =
6.4 Hz, 4 H), 0.90 (dd, J = 6.6, 4.0 Hz, 3H), 0.83 (s, J = 1.8 Hz, 9H),
0.63 (dd, J = 11.3, 6.6 Hz, 4H), 0.00 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (101
MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.9, 140.6, 133.9, 131.5, 130.9, 128.5, 123.9, 89.8,
82.6, 70.1, 69.4, 60.8, 51.6, 47.5, 37.1, 35.1, 33.7, 31.4, 27.9, 26.7,
25.9(3C), 20.2, 20.1, 18.1, 18.0, 16.1, 15.4, 12.3, - 4.5, -4.6;
