$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the Modified-Julia
Olefination: To a stirred solution of 13-BT (150 mg, 0.28 mmol, 1.0
equiv) in THF (3.2 mL) and hexamethylphosphoramide (0.8 mL) at -78 °C was
added sodium bis(trimethylsilyl)amide (1.90 M in THF, 0.180 mL, 0.34
mmol, 1.2 equiv). The resultant solution was allowed to stir at -78 °C
for 15 min followed by the rapid addition of aldehyde (0.28 mmol, 1.0
equiv in 0.5 mL THF). The mixture was allowed to reach room temperature
and stirred for an additional 6 h, at which time the reaction was
quenched by the addition of saturated ammonium chloride. The aqueous
layer was extracted with ethyl acetate and the combined organic layer was
washed with saturated sodium bicarbonate and brine and dried over
anhydrous sodium sulfate. The crude material was purified by flash
chromatography (or MPLC) on silica gel to provide the alkene products 14.
The mixture of E/Z-alkenes (ratio 80:20) was not separable by MPLC (SiO2)
and was characterized as the mixture. (3α ,5R,6β
,22E,24R)-24-Benzyloxy-6-methoxy-3,5-cyclocholest-22-ene (epi-14b-E),
yield80%; (3α ,5R,6β
,22Z,24R)-24-Benzyloxy-6-methoxy-3,5-cyclocholest-22-ene (epi-14b-Z),
yield80% (epi-14b-E): Rf 0.40 (15:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate); [α]D +48.4 (c
= 2.2, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.32-7.29 (m, 5H), 5.43 (dd, J
= 15.5, 9.0 Hz, 1H), 5.24 (dd, J = 15.5, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.58 (d, J = 12.0
Hz, 1H), 4.30 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 3.33 (s, 3H), 3.30 (dd, J = 8.5, 7.0
Hz, 1H), 2.78 (dd, J = 2.5, 2.5 Hz, 1H), 2.20-2.10 (m, 1H), 1.99 (ddd, J
= 12.5, 3.5, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.89 (ddd, J = 13.5, 3.0, 3.0 Hz, 1H),
1.81-1.62 (m, 3H), 1.61-1.50 (m, 3H), 1.43-1.40 (m, 2H), 1.35-0.80 (m,
10H), 1.09 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.03 (s, 3H), 0.95 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H),
0.86 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.75 (s, 3H), 0.65 (dd, J = 5.0, 5.0 Hz, 1H),
and 0.43 (dd, J = 7.5, 5.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 141.8,
139.3, 128.2, 127.7, 127.2, 126.6, 85.6, 82.4, 69.7, 56.6 (2C), 55.8,
48.1, 43.4, 42.8, 40.2, 40.1, 35.3, 35.1, 33.4, 33.0, 30.5, 28.9, 25.0,
24.3, 22.8, 21.5, 20.8, 19.3, 19.1, 18.6, 13.1, and 12.5; IR (thin film):
2953, 2933, 2868, 1455, 1097, 1068, 1027, 1017, 970, and 804 cm-1;
LR-EIMS [70 eV, m/z (rel. int.)] 504 (1, M+), 489 (3, M+-CH3•), and 461
(45, M+-C3H7•). (epi-14b-Z): Rf 0.45 (15:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate); [α]D
-1.7 (c 0.7 CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.37-7.33 (m, 5H), 5.46
(dd, J = 10.5, 10.5 Hz, 1H), 5.18 (dd, J = 10.5, 10.5 Hz, 1H), 4.57 (d, J
= 12.0 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1H), 3.48 (dd, J = 10.0, 6.5 Hz,
1H), 3.32 (s, 3H), 2.77 (dd, J = 3.0, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 2.46-2.38 (m, 1H),
1.96 (ddd, J = 13.0, 3.5, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.88 (ddd, J = 14.0, 3.0, 3.0 Hz,
1H), 1.81-1.62 (m, 3H), 1.61-1.50 (m, 3H), 1.43-1.40 (m, 2H), 1.35-0.80
(m, 10H), 1.09 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 1.03 (s, 3H), 0.95 (d, J = 6.5 Hz,
3H), 0.86 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.75 (s, 3H), 0.65 (dd, J = 4.5, 4.5 Hz,
1H), and 0.43 (dd, J = 8.0, 5.5 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ
141.1, 139.4, 128.2, 127.5, 127.2, 126.0, 82.4, 79.5, 69.9, 56.6, 56.5,
56.3, 48.1, 43.4, 42.9, 40.3, 35.3, 35.0, 34.7, 33.356, 33.359, 30.5,
28.6, 25.0, 24.2, 22.8, 21.6, 21.0, 19.3, 19.1, 18.7, 13.1, and 12.6; IR
(thin film): 2953, 2930, 2867, 1723, 1454, 1097, 1068, 1027, 1016, and
697 cm-1; LR-EIMS [70 eV, m/z (rel. int.)] 504 (1, M+), 489 (5, M+-CH3•),
and 461 (55, M+- C3H7•).
