$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Trityl (2S,4E,6E)-2-Vinylocta-4,6-dien-1-yl Ether (9). Under an
atmosphere of argon, KHMDS (0.5 M in toluene, 0.48 mL, 0.24 mmol) was
added dropwise to a solution of 8 (101 mg, 184 μmol) and crotonaldehyde
(23 μL, 0.28 mmol) in dry DME (2 mL) at −78 °C. The solution was allowed
to warm to rt within 16 h when no further conversion was detected [TLC:
Rf(8) = 0.34, Rf(9) = 0.80, PE/EtOAc 5:1]. Water (5 mL) was added and the
aqueous layer was separated and extracted with Et2O (2 × 30 mL). The
combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo.
Purification by flash chromatography (silica, PE/EtOAc 20:1) yielded 9 as
a oil in addition to recovered 8 (17.1 mg, 17%). The ratio E/Z = 94:6 was
determined by 1H NMR: Colorless oil, (49.6 mg, 69%). [α]20D +1.5 (c 0.81,
CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.71 (3 H, d, J = 6.4 Hz), 2.13 (1 H,
dt, J = 14.3, 7.2 Hz), 2.28−2.40 (2 H, m), 2.99−3.08 (2 H, m), 4.99−5.06
(2 H, m), 5.35−5.45 (1 H, m), 5.48−5.59 (1 H, m), 5.72 (1 H, ddd, J =
17.4, 10.5, 7.9 Hz), 5.90− 5.99 (2 H, m), 7.18−7.32 (9 H, m), 7.40−7.47
(6 H, m); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 18.2 (CH3), 34.7 (CH2), 44.7 (CH),
66.2 (CH2), 86.4 (Cq), 115.6 (CH2), 127.0 (CH), 127.2 (CH), 127.8 (CH),
128.9 (CH), 129.5 (CH), 131.7 (CH), 131.9 (CH), 140.1 (CH), 144.5 (Cq);
HR-MS (FT-ICR-ESI+) calcd for C29H30NaO [M + Na]+ 417.21889, found
417.21861.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, other preparation shown, other preparation gave lower
stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective total synthesis and absolute configuration of apiosporic
acid
