$DATUM (E)-Olefin 42. To a solution of LDA [freshly prepared from
diisopropylamine (0.05 mL, 0.36 mmol) and n-BuLi (2.7 M in n-hexane, 0.12
mL, 0.32 mmol) in THF (0.3 mL) at 0 °C for 30 min] at -78 °C was added a
solution of sulfone 41 (138.7 mg, 0.375 mmol) in THF (0.3 mL), and the
resultant solution was stirred at -78 °C for 30 min. This cold solution
was then transferred to a suspension of methyl ketone 40 (12.8 mg, 8.27
μmol) and CeCl3 (141.8 mg, 0.381 mmol) in THF (0.6 mL) at -78 °C. The
reaction mixture was gradually allowed to warm to 0 °C over 2 h before it
was diluted with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution. The mixture was
filtered through a pad of Celite, and the filtrate was extracted with
EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. Purification of the
residue by flash column chromatography (silica gel, 35% EtOAc/hexanes)
gave (E)-olefin 42 along with the corresponding (Z)-olefin. (E)-olefin
42, colorless oil, yield 7.6 mg, 53%; (Z)-olefin 42, colorless oil, yield
3.0 mg, 21%. (E)-olefin 42: [α]D 24 -3.2 (c 0.54, CH2Cl2); IR (film)
3054, 2929, 2870, 1508, 1460, 1340, 1250, 1123, 1080, 1051, 852, 836,
814, 677 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, C6D6) δ 8.05 (m, 1H), 7.80-7.57 (m, 16H),
7.51 (m, 1H), 7.47 (m, 1H), 7.42 (m, 1H), 7.30-7.22 (m, 8H), 6.10 (ddd, J
= 11.0, 11.0, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 5.62 (dd, J = 11.0, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 5.24 (d, J =
12.4 Hz, 1H), 5.13 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 5.07 (d, J = 12.4 Hz, 1H),
4.79-4.72 (m, 3H), 4.67 (d, J = 11.9 Hz, 1H), 4.55-4.44 (m, 4H), 4.26 (d,
J = 11.9 Hz, 1H), 4.16-4.07 (m, 3H), 3.70-3.62 (m, 4H), 3.57-3.52 (m,
2H), 3.50-3.40 (m, 5H), 3.38-3.32 (m, 2H), 3.30-3.14 (m, 6H), 2.96 (ddd,
J = 13.7, 13.7, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 2.90 (dd, J = 11.9, 3.4 Hz, 1H), 2.75 (m,
1H), 2.56 (dd, J = 13.7, 4.6 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (dd, J = 13.7, 10.1 Hz, 1H),
2.43-2.37 (m, 3H), 2.29 (dd, J = 11.5, 4.1 Hz, 1H), 2.23-2.09 (m, 5H),
2.08-1.98 (m, 2H), 1.97-1.64 (m, 17H), 1.60-1.44 (m, 4H), 1.33 (s, 3H),
1.28 (s, 3H), 1.23-1.21 (m, 9H), 1.15 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H), 1.07 (s, 3H),
1.00 (s, 9H), 0.88 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.064 (s, 3H), 0.061 (s, 3H); 13C
