$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM LiHMDS (17.1mL of 1.0M solution in THF, 10.3 mmol) was added to a
solution of sulfone 5 (3.0 g, 8.5 mmol) in anhydrous THF (30 mL) at -78
°C and stirred for an additional 30 min at the same temperature. To this
cold solution, aldehyde 7a (1.75 g, 10.63 mmol) in THF (20 mL) was added
and stirring continued at -78 °C. After 3 h, the mixture was quenched
with saturated NH4Cl solution and extracted with EtOAc (3×25 mL). The
combined organic layers were washed with water and saturated NaCl, dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced pressure to yield
the crude product. The residue was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography using EtOAc (5-20%) in hexanes. 4-acetyl pterostilbene
(1.35 g, 53% yield) and pterostilbene (0.42 g, 19% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, key step, Julia Olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of pterostilbene by Julia olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Peddikotla, Prabhakar; Chittiboyina, Amar G.; Khan, Ikhlas A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2013), 43(23), 3217-3223

