$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for 3-8. To a solution of 19 (43 mg, 0.078 mmol) in
anhydrous THF (260 μL) at -50 ºC was added dropwise LHMDS (78 μL, 1.0 M
in THF, 0.078 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at the same temperature
for 2 h. Next, a solution of the corresponding ketone 14 (23 mg, 0.047
mmol) in anhydrous THF (310 μL) was added dropwise to the mixture. After
being stirred at -50 ºC during 5 h, the reaction mixture was poured into
a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted with Et2O. The
combined organic fractions were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated
to give a crude which was dissolved in anhydrous MeOH (1.2 mL) and cooled
down at 0 ºC. (–)- CSA (50 mg, 0.220 mmol) was then added, and the
mixture was stirred a room temperature overnight. The reaction was
quenched by adding a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3. The aqueous
layer was extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic fractions were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated to give a crude which was purified by
column chromatography using silica gel 60 Å (32-63 μm) pH 7 and EtOAc as
eluent. The diastereoisomers were isolated by reversephase preparative
HPLC (ODS-A column, 5 μm, 250x10 mm). Conditions: 4.5 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O
(45:55) for 3 and 4; 4 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O (50:50) for 5 and 6. Retention
times: t R (3)= 28.6 min. t R (4)= 24.1 min. t R (5)= 20.7 min. t R (6)=
18.9 min. 1α,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (3). Yield: 52%.
1α,2β,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (4). Yield: 14%.
1α,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (3). 1H NMR (600.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ
0.55 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.94 (d, 3H,Me 21, 3 J HH 6.5 Hz), 1.12 (m, 1H),
1.22 (s, 6H, Me 26+Me 27), 1.3 – 1.7 (m, 18H), 1.9-2.0 (m, 2H), 2.0-2.1
(m, 2H), 2.63 (dd, 1H, H4e, |2 J HH| 12.8, 3 J HH 3.9 Hz), 2.80 (d, 1H,
H9e, |2 J HH| 12.5 Hz), 2.92 (dd, 1H, H10e, |2 J HH| 14.5, 3 J HH 3.9
Hz), 3.53 (dd, 1H, H2, 3 J HH 8.2, 2.6 Hz), 3.81 (ddd, 1H, H3, 3 J HH
13.5, 9.9, 4.9 Hz), 4.12 (br s, 1H), 5.81 (d, 1H, H7, 3 J HH 11.0 Hz) and
6.38 (d, 1H, H6, 3 J HH 11.0 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (150.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.1
(C18), 18.8 (C21), 20.8 (CH2), 22.3 (CH2), 23.5 (CH2), 27.7 (CH2), 28.9
(C9), 29.2 (C26), 29.4 (C27), 33.0 (C10), 36.1 (CH), 36.4 (CH2), 40.5
(CH), 41.9 (CH2), 44.4 (CH), 45.8 (C), 56.3 (CH), 56.6 (CH), 69.8 (C1),
71.1 (C),71.3 (C3), 80.8 (C2), 115.3 (C7), 124.7 (C6), 129.7 (C5) and
143.7 (C8) ppm. MS (EI+, m/z): 420 [M+, 20%], 402 [(M−H20)+, 25%], 237
(30), 133 (65), 91 (98) and 55 (100); HRMS (EI+, m/z) calculated for
C26H44O4 (M+): 420.3234. Found: 420.3233.
1α,2β,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (4). 1H NMR (600.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ
0.56 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.94 (d, 3H, Me 21, 3 J HH 6.8 Hz), 1.10 (m, 1H),
1.22 (s, 6H, Me 26+Me 27), 1.3 – 1.7 (m, 18H), 1.9-2.0 (m, 2H), 2.0-2.1
(m, 2H), 2.81 (d, 1H, H9e, |2 J HH| 13.1 Hz), 3.10 (dd, 1H, H10e, |2 J
HH| 13.1, 3 J HH 4.9 Hz), 3.49 (m, 1H, H2), 3.69 (ddd, 1H, H1, 3 J HH
10.9, 10.9, 4.9 Hz ), 4.08 (m, 1H, H3), 5.84 (d, 1H, H7, 3 J HH 11.3 Hz)
and 6.29 (d, 1H, H6, 3 J HH 11.3 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (150.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ
12.1 (C18), 18.8 (C21), 20.8 (CH2), 22.3 (CH2), 23.5 (CH2), 27.7 (CH2),
28.9 (C9), 29.2 (C26), 29.4 (C27), 34.1 (C10), 36.1 (CH), 36.4 (CH2),
40.5 (CH2), 41.5 (CH2), 44.4 (CH2), 45.8 (C), 56.3 (CH), 56.6 (CH), 69.8
(C3), 71.0 (C1), 115.4 (C7), 124.3 (C6), 129.6 (C5) and 142.5 (C8) ppm.
2D NMR experiments revealed the presence of two additional carbons: one
overlapped with the CDCl3 signal, corresponding to C2 (77.2 ppm according
to the HSQC), and other superimposed with the signal at 71.0 ppm,
corresponding to C25 (HMBC).
