$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (6R)-9-Benzyloxy-6-methylnon-4-enoic acid benzyl ester (1). To a chilled
solution (-78 °C for 35 min) of 4-(1-phenyl-1H-tetrazol-5-sulfonyl)
butyric acid benzyl ester 2 (173.9 mg, 0.45 mmol) in THF (3.0 mL) was
added lithium hexamethyldisilazide (1.6 M solution in THF, 0.28 mL, 0.45
mmol), and the resulting mixture stirred for 30 min at -78 °C. A
pre-cooled solution (-78 °C for 40 min) of
(2R)-5-benzyloxy-2-methylpentanal 3 (62.6 mg, 0.30 mmol) in THF (6.0 mL)
was then added via a cannula and stirred for 1.5 h at -78 °C. The mixture
was allowed to warm up to room temperature slowly and stirring was
continued for 19.5 h. This solution was cooled to 0 °C, diluted with
Et2O, and quenched with saturated aqueous NH4Cl. The aqueous phase was
then extracted with Et2O. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Purification on silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 12:1).
yield 66% (73.6 mg, 0.20 mmol, E:Z = 3.3:1). colorless oil. (300 MHz 1H
NMR); [α]D25 = -3.6 (c 0.78, CHCl3); IR (neat, cm-1) 2851, 1952, 1736,
1606, 1496, 1457, 1381, 1098, 970, 909, 736, 697, 610, 460; 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.36-7.28 (10H, m, Ph×2), 5.35-5.17 (2H, m, H10,11),
5.11 (2H, s, CH2Ph), 4.49 (2H, s, CH2Ph), 3.43 (2H, t, J = 7.3 Hz, H6),
2.44-2.29 (4H, m, H12,13), 2.08-2.00 (1H, m, H9), 1.62-1.21 (4H, m,
H7,8), 0.94 (3H, d, J = 7.3 Hz, CH3); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.2,
173.1, 138.8, 137.7, 136.2, 128.7, 128.5, 128.3, 127.8, 127.6, 126.5,
126.3, 73.0, 70.7, 66.3, 66.2, 36.7, 34.7, 34.6, 34.0, 33.5, 31.8, 28.0,
27.9, 27.7, 23.2, 21.4, 20.9; EI-HRMS (m/z) calcd for C24H30O3 [M]+
