$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D. A solution of allyl sulfone 16 (250
mg, 1.0 mmol) in DMF/TDA-1 = 3:1 (v/v) (10 mL, 0.1 M) was cooled to -60
°C, and KN(TMS)2 (0.6 M solution in toluene) (1.83 mL, 1.1 mmol) was
added dropwise within 10 s. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C
for 2 min, and aldehyde 12c (131 μL, 1.1 mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was added
dropwise. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C for 1 h before it
was allowed to warm to rt. After 6 h at rt, the reaction was terminated
and purified using the same protocol as mentioned in method A. The
reaction yielded 13c14 . Table 3, entry 72, Olefin 13e:.15,16yield 71%.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.09 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 4.22 (dd, J = 6.7,
1.3 Hz, 2H*), 4.54 (s, 2H and 2H*), 5.08-5.44 (m, 2H and 2H*), 5.66 (dt,
J = 11.8, 6.8 Hz, 1H*), 5.84 (dt, J = 14.4, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 6.19 (t, J =
11.1 Hz, 1H*), 6.26-6.45 (m, 2H), 6.60 (dt, J = 16.8, 10.6 Hz, 1H*),
7.27-7.42 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 66.0, 70.4, 72.3, 117.8,
119.4, 121.4, 122.5, 124.8, 125.1, 126.6, 128.0, 128.6, 130.3, 131.9,
132.3, 133.5, 136.5, 138.4; IR (film) ν-1 3086, 3028, 2930, 2851, 1456,
1427, 1238, 1095, 1074, 1003, 910, 756, 727; MS (CI) m/z 174 (84) [M+],
175 (20) [M++1], 149 (100), 145 (54), 133 (49), 118 (56), 117 (81), 115
(62), 105 (94); HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C12H14O 174.1039, found 174.1038.
