$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.1. General Procedure NaHMDS (1.5 equiv, 1M
or 2M in THF) was added dropwise to a solution of sulfone 6 (1 equiv) and
benzaldehyde (or 4-bromobenzaldehyde) (1.05 equiv) in THF (0.05M) at -78
°C under argon. The mixture was stirred for 30 min at -78 °C, then 3h at
room temperature, then was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by chromatography (silica, pentane/AcOEt 98:2) to
afford the corresponding fluoroalkenes. 4.2.1
(R)-1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-fluoro-3-methylpent-1-ene (1a) The general
procedure was followed with sulfone 6h (178.6 mg, 0.62 mmol),
4-bromobenzaldehyde (121 mg, 0.65 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 465 μL, 0.93
mmol) and THF (13.2 mL). 4.2.6 (2R)-3-Fluoro-2-phenyl-dodec-3-ene (1f)
The general procedure was followed with sulfone 6i (127 mg, 0.40 mmol),
nonanal (68 μL, 0.40 mmol), NaHMDS (1M in THF, 570 μL, 0.57 mmol) and THF
(8.2 mL). Yield of 1f as colorless oil, 57.8 mg (Z/E: 83/17), 58%.
(Z)-Isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.29-7.17 (m, 5H), 4.59 (dt,
3JHFcis 38.0 Hz, 3JHH 7.6 Hz, 1H), 3.52 (dq, 3JHFall 14.4 Hz, 3JHH 7.2
Hz, 1H), 2.07-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.37 (d, 3JHH 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.33-1.24 (m,
12H), 0.85 (t, 3JHH 6.8 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 161.7 (d,
1JCF 254 Hz), 142.7, 128.4 (2C), 127.3 (2C), 126.6, 105.2 (d, 2JCF 15.8
Hz), 42.4 (d, 2JCF 26.6 Hz), 31.9, 29.5 (d, 4JCF 1.1 Hz), 29.4, 29.3,
29.2, 23.5 (d, 3JCF 5.4 Hz), 22.7, 19.0 (d, 3JCF 4 Hz), 14.1 ppm. 19F NMR
(376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -112.0 (dd, 3JHFtrans38.0 Hz, 3JHFall 14.4 Hz) ppm.
(E)-Isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.29-7.17 (m, 5H), 4.99 (dt,
3JHFcis 22.8 Hz, 3JHH 8.3 Hz, 1H), 3.89 (dq, 3JHFall 31.7 Hz, 3JHH 7.5
Hz, 1H), 2.07-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.45 (d, 3JHH 7.5 Hz, 3H), 1.33-1.24 (m,
12H), 0.85 (t, 3JHH 6.8 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 161.3 (d,
1JCF 251.6 Hz), 142.4 (d, 3JCF 2.5 Hz), 128.4 (2C), 127.3 (2C), 126.5,
105.5 (d, 2JCF 21.4 Hz), 37.8 (d, 2JCF 24.7 Hz), 31.9, 30.0 (d, 4JCF 2
Hz), 29.4, 29.3, 29.2, 29.1, 25.3 (d, 3JCF 8.9 Hz), 22.7, 17.8, 14.1 ppm
19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -115.7 (dd, 3JHFcis 22.4 Hz, 3JHFall 31.6 Hz)
ppm. MS (EI)(m/z) 262.3 ((M)+., 14). HRMS (EI) for C18H27F (M).+calcd
262.20968, found 262.21043.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, NaHMDS/THF added dropwise stage 1, Julia-Kocienski
reaction
