$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for 3-8. To a solution of 19
(43 mg, 0.078 mmol) in anhydrous THF (260 μL) at -50 ºC was added
dropwise LHMDS (78 μL, 1.0 M in THF, 0.078 mmol) and the mixture was
stirred at the same temperature for 2 h. Next, a solution of the
corresponding ketone 14 (23 mg, 0.047 mmol) in anhydrous THF (310 μL) was
added dropwise to the mixture. After being stirred at -50 ºC during 5 h,
the reaction mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous solution of
NH4Cl and extracted with Et2O. The combined organic fractions were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated to give a crude which was dissolved
in anhydrous MeOH (1.2 mL) and cooled down at 0 ºC. (–)- CSA (50 mg,
0.220 mmol) was then added, and the mixture was stirred a room
temperature overnight. The reaction was quenched by adding a saturated
aqueous solution of NaHCO3. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc.
The combined organic fractions were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated to give a crude which was purified by column chromatography
using silica gel 60 Å (32-63 μm) pH 7 and EtOAc as eluent. The
diastereoisomers were isolated by reversephase preparative HPLC (ODS-A
column, 5 μm, 250x10 mm). Conditions: 4.5 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O (45:55) for 3
and 4; 4 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O (50:50) for 5 and 6. Retention times: t R (3)=
28.6 min. t R (4)= 24.1 min. t R (5)= 20.7 min. t R (6)= 18.9 min.
1α,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (3). Yield: 52%.
1β,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (5).
1α,2β,25-Trihydroxy-3-epi-19-nor-vitamin D3 (6).
1β,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (5). 1H NMR (600.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ
0.58 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.96 (d, 3H,Me 21, 3 J HH 6.6 Hz ), 1.12 (m, 1H),
1.24 (s, 6H, Me 26+Me 27), 1.3 – 1.7 (m, 18H), 1.9-2.0 (m, 2H), 2.0-2.1
(m, 2H), 2.24 (dd, 1H, H4ax, |2 J HH| 12.0, 3 J HH 12.0 Hz), 2.58 (dd,
