$DATUM Sulfonylphosphonate (1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (0.25 M) and cooled
to -78 °C. KHMDS (1.2 equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five
minutes at -78 °C, aldehyde (1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution. After
20 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C. Compound: 4b.
Yield: 30%. and Compound: 5a. Yield: 45%. Time(h): 2. 5a: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.31-7.24 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.15 (m, 3H), 6.13 (ddd, J = 4.9,
10.4 15.1 Hz, 1H), 6.05 (dd, J = 10.4, 14.8 Hz, 1H), 5.67 (dtd, J = 2.4,
6.9, 14.5 Hz, 1H), 5.52 (dt, J = 7.4, 14.8 Hz, 1H), 4.10 (m, 4H), 2.70
(t, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 2,62 (dd, J = 7.7, 22.4, 2H), 2.39 (q, 7.4 Hz, 2H),
1.31 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 141.7, 135.1 (d, J =
14.9 Hz), 133.4 (d, J = 4.3 Hz), 130.1 (d, J = 4.8 Hz), 128.4, 128.3,
125.8, 119.9 (d, J = 12.5 Hz), 61.9 (d, J = 6.7 Hz), 35.6, 34.4, 30.7 (d,
J = 139.5), 16.4 (d, J = 5.8 Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C17H25O3P
[M+H]+ 309.1614, found 309.1618; IR (thin film, cm-1) 3026, 2982, 2930,
2907, 1497, 1454, 1392, 1251, 1212, 1163, 1098, 1056, 1027, 990, 962,
843, 806, 781, 748, 700.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown (for
diethyl((2E,4E)-7-phenylhepta-2,4-dien-1-yl)phosphonate)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
