$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4.1. General Procedure NaHMDS (1.5 equiv, 1M or 2M in THF) was added
dropwise to a solution of sulfone 6 (1 equiv) and benzaldehyde (or
4-bromobenzaldehyde) (1.05 equiv) in THF (0.05M) at -78 °C under argon.
The mixture was stirred for 30 min at -78 °C, then 3h at room
temperature, then was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl and
extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by chromatography (silica, pentane/AcOEt 98:2) to
afford the corresponding fluoroalkenes. 4.2.1
(R)-1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-fluoro-3-methylpent-1-ene (1a) The general
procedure was followed with sulfone 6h (178.6 mg, 0.62 mmol),
4-bromobenzaldehyde (121 mg, 0.65 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 465 μL, 0.93
mmol) and THF (13.2 mL). Yield of 1a as colorless oil, 100 mg (Z/E:
29/71), 63%. IR (neat) 2965 (m), 2361 (s), 1339 (m), 1679 (m), 1486 (m),
1459 (m) cm-1. (Z)-Isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.47-7.73 (m, 2H),
7.37-7.34 (m, 2H), 5.43 (d, 3JHFtrans39.4 Hz, 1H), 2.47-2.24 (m, 1H),
1.69-1.38 (m, 2H), 1.19 (d, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (t, 3JHH 7.6 Hz, 3H)
ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.0 (d, 1JCF 270.1 Hz), 132.9, 131.4,
129.9, 129.8, 120.2, 103.9 (d, 2JCF 8.8 Hz), 39.3 (d, 2JCF 24.9 Hz),
26.6, 17.4, 11.6 ppm. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -107.7 (dd,
3JHFtrans39.4 Hz, 3JHFall 25.8 Hz) ppm. (E)-Isomer : 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.47-7.73 (m, 2H), 7.07 (d, 2H, 3JHH 8.1 Hz), 6.12 (d, 3JHFcis
21.7 Hz, 1H), 2.68 (dsxt, 3JHFall 33.9 Hz, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.69-1.38
(m, 2H), 1.18 (d, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (t, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 165.7 (d, 1JCF 259.1 Hz), 133.3 (d, 3JCF 14.6 Hz),
131.5, 130.2, 120.4, 106.7 (d, 2JCF 30.7 Hz), 34.8 (d, 2JCF 26.4 Hz),
26.4, 17.5, 11.9 ppm. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -113.0 (dd, 3JHFall 33.9
Hz, 3JHFcis 21.7 Hz) ppm. MS (EI)(m/z) 256.1 and 258.1 ((M)+., 16, 1:1
ratio), HRMS (EI) for C12H14F79Br M).+ calcd 256.02629, found 256.02652.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, NaHMDS/THF added dropwise stage 1, Julia-Kocienski
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ready Synthetic Access to Enantiopure Allylic α(F)-Branched Fluoroalkenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
