$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.1. General Procedure NaHMDS (1.5 equiv, 1M
or 2M in THF) was added dropwise to a solution of sulfone 6 (1 equiv) and
benzaldehyde (or 4-bromobenzaldehyde) (1.05 equiv) in THF (0.05M) at -78
°C under argon. The mixture was stirred for 30 min at -78 °C, then 3h at
room temperature, then was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by chromatography (silica, pentane/AcOEt 98:2) to
afford the corresponding fluoroalkenes. 4.2.1
(R)-1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-fluoro-3-methylpent-1-ene (1a) The general
procedure was followed with sulfone 6h (178.6 mg, 0.62 mmol),
4-bromobenzaldehyde (121 mg, 0.65 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 465 μL, 0.93
mmol) and THF (13.2 mL). 4.2.4 (3R)-1,3-Diphenyl-2-fluorobut-1-ene (1d)
The general procedure was followed with sulfone 6i (277 mg, 0.82 mmol),
benzaldehyde (88 μL, 0.87 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 615 μL, 1.23 mmol)
and THF (19 mL). Yield of 1d as colorless oil, 133 mg (Z/E: 36/64), 72%.
IR (neat) 3023 (w), 2974 (w), 2360 (s), 2339 (s), 1679 (s), 1493 (m),
1448 (m) cm-1. (Z)-Isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.51-7.47 (d, 3JHH
8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.34-7.20 (m, 8H), 5.59 (d, 3JHFtrans38.7 Hz, 1H), 3.75 (dq,
3JHFall 17.2 Hz, 3JHH 8.1 Hz, 1H), 1.55-1.24 (m, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.1 (d, 1JCF 269.3 Hz), 142.0, 133.6, 128.6, 128.5,
128.4, 128.3, 127.5, 127.2, 126.9, 105.6 (d, 2JCF 8.8 Hz), 43.3 (d, 2JCF
26.4 Hz), 18.8 (d, 3JCF 4.4 Hz) ppm. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -103.7
(dd, 3JHFtrans38.7 Hz, 3JHFall 17.2 Hz) ppm. (E)-Isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.34-7.20 (m, 10H), 6.27 (d, 3JHFcis 21.5 Hz, 1H), 4.13 (dq,
3JHFall 30.1 Hz, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.53 (d, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.5 (d, 1JCF 257.6 Hz), 142.1 (d, 3JCF 2.9 Hz),
134.0 (d, 3JCF 13.2 Hz), 128.6, 128.5, 127.2, 126.9, 126.7, 108.0 (d,
2JCF 27.8 Hz), 38.6 (d, 2JCF 24.9 Hz), 18.4 (d, 3JCF 4.4 Hz) ppm. 19F NMR
(282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -114.6 (dd, 3JHFcis 21.5 Hz, 3JHFall 30.1 Hz) ppm. MS
(EI)(m/z) 226.1 ((M)+., 61). HRMS (EI) for C16H15F (M).+calcd 226.11578,
found 226.11583.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, NaHMDS/THF added dropwise stage 1, Julia-Kocienski
reaction
